Maintainer: "Jungsup Lee" <int2dds@int2.us>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 9.0.0), ros-humble-ament-cmake, ros-humble-rcl, ros-humble-rclcpp, ros-humble-rcutils, ros-humble-rmw, ros-humble-rmw-int2dds-cpp, ros-humble-std-msgs, ros-humble-ros-workspace
Homepage: https://github.com/IntellectusCorp/int2DDS
Standards-Version: 3.9.2

Package: ros-humble-rmw-int2dds-validation
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ros-humble-rcl, ros-humble-rclcpp, ros-humble-rclpy, ros-humble-rcutils, ros-humble-rmw, ros-humble-rmw-int2dds-cpp, ros-humble-std-msgs, ros-humble-ros-workspace
Description: rclcpp and rclpy validation probes for the int2DDS RMW implementation: QoS behaviour checks (durability, history depth, deadline, liveliness, lifespan), content-filtered topic lifecycle, executor callback smoke checks and latency/throughput/readiness measurements.
 These live outside rmw_int2dds_cpp on purpose. rclcpp sits above the RMW layer (rclcpp -&gt; rcl -&gt; rmw_implementation -&gt; rmw_int2dds_cpp through the rmw_implementation_packages group), so an RMW implementation that depended on rclcpp would close a build dependency cycle. No upstream RMW does it; ros2/rmw_zenoh keeps its rclcpp-based checks in test_rmw_zenoh_cpp for the same reason.
